          "id": "RUSTSEC-2019-0009",
          "package": "smallvec",
          "title": "Double-free and use-after-free in SmallVec::grow()",
          "description": "Attempting to call `grow` on a spilled SmallVec with a value equal to the current capacity causes it to free the existing data. This performs a double free immediately and may lead to use-after-free on subsequent accesses to the SmallVec contents.\n\nAn attacker that controls the value passed to `grow` may exploit this flaw to obtain memory contents or gain remote code execution.\n\nCredits to [@ehuss](https://github.com/ehuss) for discovering, reporting and fixing the bug.",
          "date": "2019-06-06",
          "aliases": [
